Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6prm: handle GPR_BASIC_RSP_RESULT in PRM callback

Some ADSP firmware (e.g. SM6115 vendor kamorta) responds to PRM
clock and HW core requests with GPR_BASIC_RSP_RESULT (0x02001005)
instead of PRM-specific response opcodes. The firmware reports
AR_EFAILED (status=1) for clock requests that actually succeed.

Handle GPR_BASIC_RSP_RESULT by translating to the original command
opcode and forcing status to 0, matching the vendor driver behavior
of ignoring these non-critical errors.

This replaces the fire-and-forget workaround.
Based on AudioReach API:
https://github.com/AudioReach/audioreach-graphservices
---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6prm.c	2026-04-06 10:45:24
@@ -203,9 +203,31 @@
 		result = data->payload;
 		prm->result.opcode = hdr->opcode;
 		prm->result.status = result->status;
+		dev_dbg(&gdev->dev, "PRM rsp opcode=0x%08x status=%d\n",
+			hdr->opcode, result->status);
+		wake_up(&prm->wait);
+		break;
+	case GPR_BASIC_RSP_RESULT:
+		/*
+		 * Some ADSP firmware responds with
+		 * GPR_BASIC_RSP_RESULT instead of the PRM-specific response
+		 * opcodes. Translate to the request opcode so that
+		 * audioreach_send_cmd_sync() wait condition is satisfied.
+		 *
+		 * Force status to 0 because this firmware reports
+		 * AR_EFAILED for clock requests that actually succeed.
+		 * The vendor driver ignores this error.
+		 */
+		result = data->payload;
+		prm->result.opcode = result->opcode;
+		prm->result.status = 0;
+		if (result->status)
+			dev_dbg(&gdev->dev, "PRM basic rsp for cmd=0x%08x status=%d (ignored)\n",
+				result->opcode, result->status);
 		wake_up(&prm->wait);
 		break;
 	default:
+		dev_dbg(&gdev->dev, "PRM unknown opcode=0x%08x\n", hdr->opcode);
 		break;
 	}
 
